/* ---- USB ----
 *
 * The base tree's three nodes are the vendor's shape and their compatibles
 * ("mediatek,usb3", "mediatek,mt67xx-xhci", "mediatek,mt6885-phy") match nothing
 * in mainline, so they stay off and the hardware is described the mainline way
 * instead, following the working MT6895 port on this SoC generation:
 *
 *   - one mtu3 node that owns the PHY and CONTAINS the xhci as a child, because
 *     mtu3 is what calls of_platform_populate() on its children (ssusb_host_init)
 *     and what powers the PHY.  The xhci node on its own has no PHY handling at
 *     all in 7.2 (neither xhci-mtk.c nor xhci-plat.c looks at "phys").
 *   - the parent uses #address-cells/#size-cells = 2 and a ranges property, so
 *     the child's reg = <0 0 0 0x1000> lands on 0x11200000 exactly as in
 *     mt8195's ssusb0.
 *
 * Addresses: the vendor node puts everything at 0x11200000, but mainline wants
 * the MAC (mtu3) at 0x11201000 + 0x2e00 with the IPPC at 0x11203e00 + 0x100,
 * and the xhci register block at 0x11200000 + 0x1000.  The vendor tree covers
 * the same range with one 64 KiB region, so this is a split, not a new claim.
 *
 * Clocks: the vendor tree's own ids decode (against the vendor MT6885 clock
 * header) to INFRACFG_AO_SSUSB_CG and INFRACFG_AO_SSUSB_XHCI_CG - our mainline
 * gates CLK_INFRA_AO_SSUSB and CLK_INFRA_AO_SSUSB_XHCI, both muxed through
 * usb_sel / ssusb_xhci_sel which the mainline topckgen driver provides.  The
 * MT6895 port used <&clk26m> for sys_ck; the real gates are used here because
 * they exist, and because an enable count in clk_summary is evidence.
 *
 * PHY: the MT6895 port matches "mediatek,mt6785-tphy" plus the generic-v2
 * fallback, which is what actually binds (there is no mt6785 entry in
 * phy-mtk-tphy's id table).  Only the USB2 port is described; the port only
 * wires u2port.  The u2 tuning values are chopin's own, from the base tree's
 * usb_phy_tuning node, mapped onto the property names phy-mtk-tphy parses
 * (u2_vrt_ref -> eye-vrt, u2_term_ref -> eye-term, u2_intr_cal -> intr,
 * u2_discth -> discth; u2_enhance has no mainline equivalent and is dropped).
 *
 * The vendor PHY node must stay disabled rather than be reused: phy-mtk-tphy
 * walks *all* children (for_each_child_of_node_scoped, not _available_) and
 * fails the whole probe on a child without a reg, which the base tree's
 * usb_phy_tuning child would be.
 */
